WEBVTT

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:53.880
<i>Gramps died.</i>

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:58.620
<i>If he'd hung in there a little longer,
he would've seen another spring.</i>

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:08.350
Setsu!

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:09.840
Wait!

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:11.840
Setsu, stop!

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:13.090
Where do you plan on going?

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:17.260
Somewhere loud.

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:19.190
Loud?

00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:21.520
How am I meant to work it out from that?

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:24.190
Oh. Then, Tokyo.

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:26.720
You... You decided that
just now, didn't you?

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:27.190
Yup.

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:30.790
I know Gramps' passing has been rough on you.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:31.940
But even so...

00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:34.140
When Gramps...

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:38.490
When Gramps died, my sound disappeared, too.

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:43.370
The sound I love isn't here anymore.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:47.020
There's nothing here anymore.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:53.170
Those Snow

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:53.170
White Notes

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:05.810
Episode 1
Desolate

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:06.350
<i>Oh, Yuna-chan?</i>

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:09.680
<i>So about that direct-to-vid audition
the other day... I'm sorry, but...</i>

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:11.070
I didn't get the part?

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:15.250
<i>Ah, but we're still waiting to hear back on that
late-night show, Bewitching Musical Revue.</i>

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:17.410
I'll get that one! I'm sure of it.

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:19.360
<i>Oh, that's a nice, positive attitude!</i>

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:21.050
Um, yes...

00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:23.870
We've been waiting for you!

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:25.340
Hello.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:27.490
<i>Even at times like these, I have to smile. Smile.</i>

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.930
This is his first time
coming to a place like this.

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:29.920
<i>It's so disheartening.</i>

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:31.260
<i>I've got no money.</i>

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:31.260
H-Hello.

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:32.990
<i>But I've got determination.</i>

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:32.990
Nice to meet you!

00:02:32.990 --> 00:02:34.660
<i>As for talent...</i>

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:36.260
Now, drink up! Drink up!

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:36.250
<i>I'd like to think I have that, too.</i>

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:40.270
See you again sometime! Good night!

00:02:40.270 --> 00:02:42.030
Yes, come back soon!

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:44.140
Take care! Good night!

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:48.080
<i>Men.</i>

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:52.980
Taketo

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:52.980
Waaah

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:52.980
They've got no eye for talent. They're morons.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:52.980
If they can't see your charms, Yuna,

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:52.980
you're better off not getting it.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:52.980
You're
No. 1

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:52.990
<i>Though, I've got a man who's talented.</i>

00:02:52.990 --> 00:02:56.990
Aw, Taketo! You're such a sweetie!

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:16.230
Sorry. I'm feeling a little intoxicated.

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:17.920
What? Too much to drink?

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:19.260
No, it's the lights.

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:20.950
The lights?

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:25.960
<i>That guy's a walking hazard...</i>

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:31.610
Boss!

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:33.530
What? That idiot!

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:34.700
You all right?

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:36.320
Damn wino!

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:41.030
You piece of crap.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:49.080
You slut!

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:50.330
Shut up!

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:03.130
Why, Gramps?!

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:05.070
Why won't you teach me it?

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:09.130
It's not just you. I'm not
teaching that piece to anyone.

00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:10.700
You rotten old man!

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:13.870
Well, there's nothing to learn
from a "rotten old man," is there?

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:17.060
Sound.

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:19.960
Use your own sound to steal it.

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:23.160
Setsu.

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:27.790
If I die, stop playing the shamisen.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:45.310
Gramps...

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:49.230
It's cold.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:54.880
Oh, you're up?

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:57.350
You hurting anywhere?

00:04:57.350 --> 00:05:00.000
Honestly. You need to be more careful.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.110
There's a lot of rough types in that area.

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:05.530
Tachiki Yuna

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:05.990
Tachiki Yuna

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:06.570
Tachiki Yuna

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:06.740
Tachiki Yuna

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:10.620
What... is this?

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:12.440
Cute, isn't it?

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:15.510
My boyfriend left some of his clothes here,
but he'd get mad if I lent them to you.

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:19.960
He'd probably chastise you more for
putting me up than for lending me clothes.

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:23.780
Are you from abroad?

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:24.960
I'm Japanese.

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:32.870
Is that a guitar?
The case looks sort of different.

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:36.430
It's a Tsugaru shamisen.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:40.040
Wow, really? My boyfriend plays guitar.

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:41.360
Play me something.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:42.480
No.

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:44.600
I can't.

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:49.150
So, uh, what were you doing
in Roppongi, anyway?

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:50.410
Nothing, really.

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:53.910
There was nothing left for me back home.

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:57.440
I'm empty inside right now.

00:05:57.980 --> 00:06:02.420
I feel like I need something,
so I'm out looking for it.

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:07.640
Empty, huh?

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:11.180
Okay!

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:12.290
How does this sound?

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:15.270
You can stay here till you find out what
you wanna do and where you wanna go.

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:16.000
Huh?

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:19.200
And no funny business or my
boyfriend will kill you, you got that?

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:20.400
I would never!

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.190
And in exchange, you can do all the housework.

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:26.400
<i>Wakana-niichan, Tokyo is a strange place.</i>

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:24.060
Huh? What” Eh?

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:26.400
Hawaii? You want to go to Hawaii?

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:30.400
<i>Gramps.</i>

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:33.570
<i>It's already been a week since Setsu left.</i>

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:39.040
<i>Out of the two of us, the brother who's
inherited your talent for shamisen...</i>

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:41.230
<i>is Setsu, without a doubt.</i>

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:45.340
<i>As soon as he was old enough to
understand, he loved that sound,</i>

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:47.500
<i>and he's been chasing it ever since.</i>

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:52.190
<i>Now that Gramps is gone,
the sound is gone, too.</i>

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:55.060
<i>He's lost everything.</i>

00:06:56.070 --> 00:06:58.490
<i>Without Gramps' sound, even I...</i>

00:06:58.960 --> 00:06:59.880
Wakana-chan!

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:02.140
A letter from Setsu!

00:07:02.140 --> 00:07:03.720
Huh? Eh? Give it here!

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:16.660
Wakana-niichan

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:18.660
Tokyo is a strange place.

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:18.660
I met a girl who said I could

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:18.660
stay with her for a while.

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:18.660
She's Tachiki Yuna-san.

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:18.660
She's 22 years old.

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:18.660
Apparently,
she's a pin-up girl.

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:09.180
<i>Wakana-niichan, Tokyo is a strange place.</i>

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:13.160
<i>I met a girl who said I could
stay with her for a while.</i>

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:16.210
<i>She's Tachiki Yuna-san. She's 22 years old.</i>

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:18.660
<i>Apparently, she's a pin-up girl.</i>

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:19.740
Hey.

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:26.010
Is Tokyo so full of pin-up girls that
it's easy to end up living with one?

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:28.670
What are you talking about? Of course not.

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:30.180
I didn't think so.

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:32.080
Setsu!

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:34.200
Is that what you went to Tokyo for?!

00:07:35.420 --> 00:07:37.510
This is Setsu-kun, the kid I told you about.

00:07:37.820 --> 00:07:38.810
Hold up.

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:41.030
When you said you took in
a kid you felt sorry for...

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:43.830
I thought you meant an
<i>actual</i> kid, not some regular guy!

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:45.020
Hey, take it easy.

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:49.020
Are you Yuna-san's "talented" boyfriend?

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:54.130
Killer voice, killer guitar skills,
and killer looks. The name's Taketo.

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:56.130
I'm the guy carrying this band.

00:07:56.130 --> 00:07:57.710
Right, my supporting characters?

00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:02.150
Okay, everyone! It's my treat tonight.

00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:06.170
You're working toward your major label debut,
so eat lots, and build up your stamina!

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:08.080
All right!

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:10.340
Thanks for the food!

00:08:14.990 --> 00:08:16.340
<i>A week.</i>

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:18.470
<i>It's already been a week.</i>

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:22.800
<i>This is the first time I've gone
this long without playing it.</i>

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:23.980
Sorry, Yuna.

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:25.740
The money for renting the studio...

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:26.750
Oh, right.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:29.720
Huh? Is this all?

00:08:29.720 --> 00:08:30.780
I'm sorry.

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:33.290
I haven't gotten my paycheck yet.

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:38.830
I don't think there's any reason
for you to be doing that, Yuna-san.

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:43.090
It's not like I'm just <i>giving</i> it to him.

00:08:43.090 --> 00:08:44.830
I'm supporting his talent.

00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:47.770
Even though just being there
should be support enough?

00:08:47.770 --> 00:08:50.140
Is this really something
you want to do, Yuna-san?

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:53.310
Of course she does! Right?

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:56.600
What's up? Something wrong?

00:08:57.400 --> 00:09:00.190
Man. You totally killed the mood.

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:01.350
Go home before I kill <i>you</i>.

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:04.350
Yeah, I'm starting to want to
kill you, too, so I'm going.

00:09:05.530 --> 00:09:07.850
Piece of crap! Who do you think you are?!

00:09:05.780 --> 00:09:07.850
Taketo! Stop it! Taketo!

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:10.210
Quit acting like a spoiled brat!

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:11.200
Calm down!

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:11.200
Let go of me!

00:09:16.190 --> 00:09:17.190
<i>Disgraceful.</i>

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:18.950
Don't use a smart phone when you're walking!

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:18.950
Please calm down, sir.

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:24.710
<i>Tokyo is noisy.</i>

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:27.370
<i>You don't hear sounds. You hear voices.</i>

00:09:28.140 --> 00:09:31.120
<i>Gramps, can't I play yet?</i>

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:34.720
<i>Is my sound that disgraceful?</i>

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:35.970
Setsu.

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:39.230
You play the shamisen well.

00:09:39.230 --> 00:09:43.270
But the truth is, you only ever imitate me.

00:09:43.630 --> 00:09:46.430
But I <i>want</i> to sound like you, Gramps.

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:48.980
Pass your impromptu on to me.

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:51.790
Disgraceful.

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:52.920
Setsu.

00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:57.240
If I die, stop playing the shamisen.

00:09:58.590 --> 00:10:02.560
Until you realize how you sound so disgraceful,

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:04.360
you are not allowed to play it.

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:10.910
<i>It took Gramps thirty years to complete his
impromptu piece, "Shungyou (Spring Dawn)."</i>

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:18.630
There's no way I'd be able to play it.

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:20.440
Still...

00:10:21.080 --> 00:10:23.360
This is the first time I've felt like this.

00:10:25.050 --> 00:10:27.230
I want to play the shamisen.

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:30.140
Okay, we're going now.

00:10:30.140 --> 00:10:31.480
'Kay.

00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:36.270
Taketo, I failed another audition.

00:10:36.270 --> 00:10:37.320
Yeah?

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:40.520
I'm kinda feeling like I just
want to give up, you know?

00:10:40.520 --> 00:10:42.250
What're you talking about?

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:44.880
No woman shines brighter than you, Yuna.

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:46.300
Have more faith in yourself.

00:10:46.650 --> 00:10:47.690
Yeah...

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:51.130
Hey. Are you free after this?

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:53.470
Huh? Oh, sorry...

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:55.580
I wanted to write some music tonight.

00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:56.300
Oh, okay.

00:10:57.150 --> 00:10:58.550
Work hard, then.

00:11:04.960 --> 00:11:07.550
Lessons in the afternoon
and a part-time job at night...

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:09.360
I'm exhausted.

00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:12.650
I'm so tired... I just can't...

00:11:15.410 --> 00:11:16.890
Setsu-kun?

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:25.400
Setsu-kun!

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:51.470
I didn't get it? But I was so
confident about that audition!

00:11:51.470 --> 00:11:55.560
And well, you see, we got
this <i>other</i> offer for you...

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:57.570
Living With Yuna

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:57.570
100% Exposed

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:57.570
(Tentative Title)

00:11:56.830 --> 00:11:57.570
Huh?

00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:03.870
In the world of adult entertainment,
your face and body would be powerful weapons.

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:07.450
Don't mess with me. Go die.

00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:08.700
I'll tell you this much:

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:11.410
the agency's just <i>waiting</i> for you to quit!

00:12:20.570 --> 00:12:22.040
<i>It's all right.</i>

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:23.800
<i>It's not like I've got nothing.</i>

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:25.830
<i>After all, I have him.</i>

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:39.030
You can have him.

00:12:39.030 --> 00:12:40.770
I don't need him.

00:12:47.590 --> 00:12:49.800
<i>My fingers are rusty.</i>

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:51.550
<i>That was terrible.</i>

00:12:52.180 --> 00:12:53.040
<i>But...</i>

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:55.390
<i>It felt amazing.</i>

00:13:01.890 --> 00:13:02.720
Welcome back.

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:08.690
Yuna-san, I'm sorry about yesterday.

00:13:09.420 --> 00:13:12.720
I had no right to get involved.

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:16.730
I heard you playing the shamisen
on the riverbank.

00:13:17.800 --> 00:13:18.800
Did you?

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:22.370
Yuna-san... Thank you.

00:13:22.370 --> 00:13:26.100
If I hadn't met you, I never would've
played it. I would've just kept running.

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:29.700
Setsu-kun... I...

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:34.750
I thought you were like me, a sad person
with nothing going for you.

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:35.790
That's why I let you stay.

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:38.880
But now...

00:13:39.760 --> 00:13:41.300
I'm jealous of you.

00:13:42.410 --> 00:13:46.560
So I'm sorry, but I'm going
to go away for a while.

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:49.050
Please leave in the meantime.

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:02.110
To Yuna-san,

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:02.110
I put the fish and meat in the freezer.

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:02.110
Please eat the kinpira

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:02.110
in plastic container

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:02.110
by the 13th.

00:14:00.680 --> 00:14:04.280
<i>I feel like I haven't got many memories.</i>

00:14:04.590 --> 00:14:06.480
<i>And like I've got lots of them.</i>

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:07.990
Tachiki

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:13.460
Hey, you! The spoiled brat!

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:16.590
Where's Yuna?

00:14:19.580 --> 00:14:21.720
Seriously, she's not picking up her phone.

00:14:21.720 --> 00:14:23.440
And she's not replying to my texts.

00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:24.810
You <i>sure</i> you don't know anything?

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:27.390
I thought she went to your place.

00:14:28.650 --> 00:14:30.640
Well, she did come over, but...

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:32.100
The timing wasn't great.

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:34.280
Seriously? <i>Another</i> groupie?

00:14:34.280 --> 00:14:36.280
It's her fault for showing up unannounced!

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:37.930
You reap what you sow.

00:14:38.720 --> 00:14:40.650
What would <i>you</i> know?!

00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:43.400
Yuna and I work hard to
achieve our dreams together!

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:46.090
Then, why are you sleeping around?

00:14:46.090 --> 00:14:50.410
Yuna-san works hard day and night to
make up for all the stuff you <i>don't</i> do.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:53.580
You haven't worked hard at all.
Quit acting so full of yourself!

00:14:55.420 --> 00:14:56.910
I see how it is.

00:15:00.050 --> 00:15:02.510
Taketo! That's enough!

00:15:02.510 --> 00:15:03.930
We should be on stage by now

00:15:03.930 --> 00:15:04.840
Shut up!

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:07.840
Taketo! Taketo!

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:09.710
I'm the one the fans are waiting for!

00:15:09.710 --> 00:15:12.140
You should be working on improving
my mood before I go out there!

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:15.480
You're a real scumbag.

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:21.630
I sent Yuna a message earlier, saying if
she didn't show up, I'd break your arm.

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:22.730
Time to make good on my word.

00:15:27.850 --> 00:15:30.490
Wow, look at you, all panicked.

00:15:30.890 --> 00:15:34.240
Acting mad at me when really
it's the kid you've got feelings forвЂ”

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:36.220
Karma Kick!

00:15:36.630 --> 00:15:38.520
Yu... Yuna...

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:40.380
You...

00:15:40.570 --> 00:15:43.050
Setsu-kun, I'm sorry you
got caught up in this.

00:15:43.050 --> 00:15:45.540
This reminds me of how we first met.

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:46.890
Taketo! Can you still go on stage?

00:15:46.890 --> 00:15:48.070
Now I'm <i>pissed</i>.

00:15:48.070 --> 00:15:49.630
Go on stage?

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:50.750
Why should I care?!

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:52.700
You're going to betray your fans?

00:15:52.700 --> 00:15:53.820
Shut up!

00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:55.130
It's got nothing to do with you.

00:15:57.350 --> 00:15:58.270
Setsu-kun.

00:15:58.270 --> 00:15:59.010
Huh?

00:15:59.450 --> 00:16:02.760
Sorry about this, but can you stay
caught up in this a little while longer?

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:06.690
Taketo! Taketo!

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:09.900
Taketo! Take Huh?

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:10.890
Who's that?

00:16:13.920 --> 00:16:15.630
Um...

00:16:15.630 --> 00:16:17.850
I'm the... opening act.

00:16:17.850 --> 00:16:19.680
Just until the main act shows up.

00:16:19.680 --> 00:16:22.250
It's a bit of a different genre.
Sorry about that.

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:23.740
I'll be playing "Jongara Bushi."

00:16:23.740 --> 00:16:25.690
Wait, Yuna-chan...

00:16:25.690 --> 00:16:28.880
Please don't upset Taketo
any more than he already is.

00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:33.500
What is this? Where's Taketo?

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:36.180
Hurry up and bring Taketo out!

00:16:44.960 --> 00:16:46.010
<i>Gramps.</i>

00:16:46.490 --> 00:16:49.380
<i>Will I be able to play well?</i>

00:16:50.880 --> 00:16:51.780
Setsu.

00:16:52.760 --> 00:16:56.080
You see, I love the spring.

00:16:56.640 --> 00:17:00.320
But that doesn't mean I hate the winter.

00:17:00.940 --> 00:17:04.400
First, the Tsugaru winter
freezes everything.

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:10.110
Then, the sun comes out and,
little by little, it starts melting the snow,

00:17:10.110 --> 00:17:11.580
and the sound changes.

00:17:16.610 --> 00:17:18.550
<i>It's just like before.</i>

00:17:18.940 --> 00:17:21.540
<i>The sound makes my heart hurt.</i>

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:22.770
<i>And yet...</i>

00:17:26.300 --> 00:17:27.140
<i>Hold up.</i>

00:17:27.680 --> 00:17:30.630
<i>How can just the sound of
that kid's shamisen playing</i>

00:17:30.630 --> 00:17:32.390
<i>captive an audience like that?</i>

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:39.320
"Jongara" is truly mysterious.

00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:44.450
The older you get, the more difficult it seems.

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:49.730
I could spend my whole life
listening to this sound.

00:17:51.470 --> 00:17:54.100
The beginning is passionate. Hot-blooded.

00:17:54.590 --> 00:17:56.700
Then, it starts to calm.

00:17:57.890 --> 00:18:00.470
Little by little, it grows sadder.
More heartrending.

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:03.400
It weakens and wanes.

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:09.320
But it claws its way up again,
refusing to be beaten down.

00:18:10.070 --> 00:18:11.480
And in the end...

00:18:12.060 --> 00:18:15.230
it just keeps striking,
like it's issuing a challenge.

00:18:26.190 --> 00:18:28.880
"Jongara" is freedom.

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:30.520
Now, Setsu.

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:35.420
What kind of sound will you give it?

00:19:42.280 --> 00:19:43.910
That was awesome!

00:19:53.700 --> 00:19:55.910
I guess no one needs me.

00:19:55.910 --> 00:19:57.900
What are you sulking about?

00:19:58.530 --> 00:20:01.370
Hey. Is it over between us?

00:20:01.850 --> 00:20:02.800
Yes.

00:20:03.280 --> 00:20:06.800
Man. I lost myself a good woman.

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:10.600
A good woman, huh?

00:20:20.170 --> 00:20:25.990
<i>After that, I searched for my impression
of "sound" over and over in my mind.</i>

00:20:25.990 --> 00:20:31.200
Kawasaki Real Estate

00:20:26.570 --> 00:20:28.920
What's "key money"?

00:20:29.480 --> 00:20:31.210
What should I do...

00:20:31.610 --> 00:20:33.740
<i>Right now, no matter how much I play,</i>

00:20:33.740 --> 00:20:36.220
<i>the sound I get is dull.</i>

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:41.770
<i>I've really hit a brick wall...</i>

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:46.340
Huh?

00:20:46.650 --> 00:20:47.980
Welcome back!

00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:50.270
Why are you always here, Taketo?

00:20:50.270 --> 00:20:52.730
This place is relaxing.

00:20:52.730 --> 00:20:54.140
Oh. Make me some coffee.

00:20:55.870 --> 00:20:58.110
The lease is up on this
place this month, right?

00:20:58.110 --> 00:20:59.620
What are you gonna do?

00:21:00.850 --> 00:21:03.970
Oh. How long will it be before you're back?

00:21:03.970 --> 00:21:06.240
Well... I haven't set a date.

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:08.360
Then, will it be a long time?

00:21:08.360 --> 00:21:10.000
I think so, yes.

00:21:10.970 --> 00:21:12.110
Setsu-kun.

00:21:12.110 --> 00:21:13.050
Yeah?

00:21:13.050 --> 00:21:16.500
I quit my agency.

00:21:16.990 --> 00:21:20.380
You understand, right? I gave up on showbiz.

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:21.580
Yeah.

00:21:22.350 --> 00:21:23.770
But...

00:21:23.770 --> 00:21:26.510
Do you think this means I'm running away?

00:21:26.990 --> 00:21:28.390
Do you have any regrets?

00:21:30.220 --> 00:21:31.440
Nope!

00:21:31.440 --> 00:21:33.690
I was always empty, right from the very start.

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:37.440
I'm the one with nothing.
You know that, right?

00:21:40.610 --> 00:21:43.190
Hey, are you really not coming

00:21:51.210 --> 00:21:52.670
Yuna-san!

00:21:55.360 --> 00:21:58.360
<i>Whatever girl ends up with you, Setsu-kun...</i>

00:21:58.360 --> 00:21:59.710
<i>...will be very happy.</i>

00:22:08.030 --> 00:22:09.210
Hey!

00:22:09.210 --> 00:22:11.090
I've been meaning to ask you...

00:22:11.890 --> 00:22:14.030
Do you have any goals or anything?

00:22:14.030 --> 00:22:17.800
When you play your shamisen, you come alive,

00:22:17.800 --> 00:22:20.100
but other times, you don't
seem like you're living at all.

00:22:22.020 --> 00:22:24.670
I mean, this is just a guess,

00:22:24.670 --> 00:22:27.540
but if it's the shamisen that gives you life,

00:22:27.540 --> 00:22:31.950
then one day, whether you like it
or not, that world will drag you in.

00:22:31.950 --> 00:22:35.450
I'm not interested in anything
other than playing how I like!

00:22:36.530 --> 00:22:37.470
Setsu!

00:22:38.640 --> 00:22:40.460
Setsu! I know you're in there!

00:22:40.820 --> 00:22:42.710
U-Umeko?

00:22:42.710 --> 00:22:44.000
Charge.

00:22:51.470 --> 00:22:53.280
Baby-chan.

00:22:53.890 --> 00:22:56.990
Mama's here to pick you up.
